  "question": {
    "text": "If $\\mathrm{z}$ and $\\omega$ are two non-zero complex numbers such that $|z \\omega|=1$ and $\\operatorname{Arg}(z)-\\operatorname{Arg}(\\omega)=\\frac{\\pi}{2}$, then $\\bar{z} \\omega$ is equal to",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "FZRwQ",
      "text": "\n$-\\mathrm{i}$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "4iwNx",
      "text": "\n1\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JBmLL",
      "text": "\n$-1$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "pieRI",
      "text": "\ni.",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "$|z \\omega|=1$    <img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/TuMhRqFvtS40ZwPsoKyC5qCeDD_jVvNeN0qS7WCy7-8.original.fullsize.png\"><br>\n$$\n\\text { As, } \\operatorname{Arg}\\left(\\frac{z}{\\omega}\\right)=\\frac{\\pi}{2} \\text { therefore } \\frac{z}{\\omega}=i\n$$\n$\\therefore\\left|\\frac{z}{\\omega}\\right|=1$<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/omZ6fg5NNW1gEPTi0tsCc2HjgDIm55Br5R3waH7stuc.original.fullsize.png\"><br>\nFrom (1) \\& (2), $|z|=|\\omega|=1$ and $\\frac{z}{\\omega}+\\frac{\\bar{z}}{\\omega}=0 ; z \\bar{\\omega}+\\bar{z} \\omega=0$\n$\\bar{z} \\omega=-z \\bar{\\omega}=\\frac{-z}{\\omega} \\cdot \\bar{\\omega} \\cdot \\omega ; \\bar{z} \\omega=-i|\\omega|^2=-\\mathrm{i}$",
    "image": null
  },
